#. Column guide: Item.
msgctxt "table.help.name"
msgid "Display name on warframe.market. Click to open the listing."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Own.
msgctxt "table.help.owned"
msgid "How many copies you own in your inventory. When the \"Keep copies\" reserve is set above 0, the sellable count (owned minus the reserve) shows alongside it. Leveled copies (any XP) can’t be traded in-game at all, so they’re held back the same way - shown as \"leveled\" rather than \"kept\"."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Δ.
msgctxt "table.help.delta"
msgid "Change in count vs. the previous inventory you loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Δ.
msgctxt "table.help.delta.dir"
msgid "positive = farmed, negative = sold"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Avg.
msgctxt "table.help.avg_price"
msgid "Volume-weighted average across closed trades in the last 48 h."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Avg.
msgctxt "table.help.avg_price.dir"
msgid "noisy on low-volume items"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Low ask.
msgctxt "table.help.low_sell"
msgid "Lowest current ask: the cheapest sell listing from in-game / online players."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Low ask.
msgctxt "table.help.low_sell.dir"
msgid "what you can realistically clear at right now"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Top buy.
msgctxt "table.help.top_buy"
msgid "Highest current buy offer from in-game / online players."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Top buy.
msgctxt "table.help.top_buy.dir"
msgid "instant-sell ceiling"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Vol 48h.
msgctxt "table.help.volume_48h"
msgid "Trades closed in the last 48 h."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Vol 48h.
msgctxt "table.help.volume_48h.dir"
msgid "higher = more liquid; ≥ 5 is healthy"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Demand.
msgctxt "table.help.ratio"
msgid "Live buyers ÷ live sellers - a rough demand signal."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Demand.
msgctxt "table.help.ratio.dir"
msgid "> 1 = buyers outnumber sellers"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Stack value.
msgctxt "table.help.potential_plat"
msgid "Sellable copies × the 48 h average trade price. Optimistic - selling many copies usually clears below the average."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Stack value.
msgctxt "table.help.potential_plat.dir"
msgid "upper bound, not realistic"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Raw value.
msgctxt "table.help.raw_value"
msgid "Sellable copies × the average of the ~5 cheapest live asks (the highlighted @ price). What the stack is worth at current listings - no liquidity discount; one troll listing barely moves it."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Raw value.
msgctxt "table.help.raw_value.dir"
msgid "falls back to Sellable × Avg until the next scrape adds ask-depth data"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Priority. Keep the formula as written.
msgctxt "table.help.sell_score"
msgid "Priority ranking, not expected plat/day. Base = min(sellable owned, max(0.05, vol_48h / 2)) × clearing price; DE usage then applies a bounded 0.75×–1.25× weight. Missing or invalid usage is neutral. The clearing price is the lowest live ask, clamped up to the 90-day median when that ask is a lone troll undercut, so one 1p listing cannot sink a row. Items below 3 trades / 48 h keep their priority and get a \"patience\" tag, but stay out of Top Picks."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Priority.
msgctxt "table.help.sell_score.dir"
msgid "higher = list sooner; actual plat totals stay unweighted"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Ducats.
msgctxt "table.help.ducats"
msgid "Ducat value at Baro Ki’Teer."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Ducats.
msgctxt "table.help.ducats.dir"
msgid "only prime parts have a non-zero value"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: p/100d.
msgctxt "table.help.plat_per_100d"
msgid "Plat cost per 100 ducats of value. “Deal” badge fires below 20."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read p/100d.
msgctxt "table.help.plat_per_100d.dir"
msgid "lower = better ducat trade than WFM"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Trend.
msgctxt "table.help.medians_7d"
msgid "Sparkline of the last 7 days of daily median price. Hover the line for the raw values."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Δ 90d.
msgctxt "table.help.delta_90d_pct"
msgid "Latest daily median vs the 90-day median."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Δ 90d.
msgctxt "table.help.delta_90d_pct.dir"
msgid "▲ = price rising into a peak (sell now); ▼ = sliding"
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: Advice.
msgctxt "table.help.advice"
msgid "Hold-or-sell call from the prime calendar (release decay, Resurgence reprints, post-vault ramps) plus the year of price history. Hover a chip for the exact numbers behind it. Advice only - nothing is automated."
msgstr ""

#. Column guide: how to read Advice.
msgctxt "table.help.advice.dir"
msgid "sell now = timing favors listing; hold = the ramp is still ahead"
msgstr ""

